                                <comments>
                            <comment id="17271479" author="mmuzaf" created="Mon, 25 Jan 2021 16:30:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The issue has moved to the next release. Please, let me know if we still should include it to the 2.10&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17272857" author="timonin.maksim" created="Wed, 27 Jan 2021 13:30:21 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alex_pl&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alex_pl&quot;&gt;alex_pl&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=Pavlukhin&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;Pavlukhin&quot;&gt;Pavlukhin&lt;/a&gt;!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ve investigated this ticket and found that commit for &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-11933&quot; title=&quot;Build scalar scaladoc only if javadoc profile is active&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-11933&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-11933&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is incorrect and broke scaladoc generation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The javadoc maven plugin is declared in parent/pom.xml without profile definition&#160;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&#160;and then it applies on all modules. So&#160;javadocs are generated for all modules on the package phase and this does not depend on any profile;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Scaladocs are generated on package phase only with enabled the javadoc profile;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The javadoc profile is defined in pom.xml &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;2&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&#160;and used only for javadoc:aggregate goal. It just collects generated javadocs for the root project. Also this action performed on validate phase that performed before compile.&#160;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Release process steps after &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-11933&quot; title=&quot;Build scalar scaladoc only if javadoc profile is active&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-11933&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-11933&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; are:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;`mvn deploy -Pall-java,all-scala,licenses` that generates javadocs for all java modules &lt;b&gt;but not for the scalar modules&lt;/b&gt;;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;`mvc initialize -Pjavadoc` aggregates all created javadocs.&#160;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Also commit for &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-11933&quot; title=&quot;Build scalar scaladoc only if javadoc profile is active&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-11933&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-11933&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; does not mute scaladocs generation for the visor-console project, and they are still generated on package state.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=Pavlukhin&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;Pavlukhin&quot;&gt;Pavlukhin&lt;/a&gt;&#160; What is a purpose of muting scaladocs docs? Can we revert the patch and fix it in different way?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/blob/master/parent/pom.xml#L762&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/blob/master/parent/pom.xml#L762&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;2&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/blob/master/pom.xml#L166&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/blob/master/pom.xml#L166&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17272964" author="pavlukhin" created="Wed, 27 Jan 2021 16:12:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=timonin.maksim&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;timonin.maksim&quot;&gt;timonin.maksim&lt;/a&gt;, thank you for investigating this! I do not remember all details. I suppose there were issues with other jobs using different profile combinations. They were unable to proceed due to unneeded (for them) scaladoc step. Or perhaps the goal was to reduce build time. Is it really to good to create javadocs on &lt;em&gt;prepare-package&lt;/em&gt; phase? I would think about javadocs creation when some kind of &lt;em&gt;release&lt;/em&gt; profile is active.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17273428" author="timonin.maksim" created="Thu, 28 Jan 2021 09:07:51 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=Pavlukhin&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;Pavlukhin&quot;&gt;Pavlukhin&lt;/a&gt; ,&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alex_pl&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alex_pl&quot;&gt;alex_pl&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ve tried some ways to fix this and find that it&apos;s not easy to just move javadoc generation to different profile or phase. There are some issues, for example:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Javadoc depends on ignite-tools class&#160;org.apache.ignite.tools.javadoc.IgniteLinkTaglet. Maven requires to have a packaged jar for ignite-tools for running javadoc profile. It&apos;s due to maven dependency management. So we can&apos;t move all to prepare-package phase.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;If we run `mvn package -Pjavadoc` then it leads to some strange issues: ignite-cassandra-store module fails; number of files in root javadoc directory is bigger then after `mvn initialize -Pjavadoc` command. It&apos;s required to make more investigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;p&gt;But I think we can do it in different way. I propose to add a profile &quot;skip-docs&quot; that disables generation of docs. I&apos;ve successfully implemented this configuration. It&apos;s pretty simple and does not require changes for current release process. Also it provides a real benefit for a build time or skipping all docs for users or customers who need it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If nobody have objections I will prepare a PR for that.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17273638" author="mmuzaf" created="Thu, 28 Jan 2021 13:31:20 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=timonin.maksim&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;timonin.maksim&quot;&gt;timonin.maksim&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As I understand correctly these docs are used for the release and currently due to some issues scaladoc are note published automatically during the release steps. Why we should skip everything?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I propose to remove `IgniteLinkTaglet` at all (AFAIK it has some issues for java 8/11 compilation)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17273755" author="timonin.maksim" created="Thu, 28 Jan 2021 13:59:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=mmuzaf&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;mmuzaf&quot;&gt;mmuzaf&lt;/a&gt;&#160;hi! I proposed a new profile for skipping docs for some users if it is needed for them (purpose of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-11933&quot; title=&quot;Build scalar scaladoc only if javadoc profile is active&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-11933&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-11933&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; ticket). By default this profile should be disabled and then all docs will be generated in release process.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;gt;&#160; I propose to remove `IgniteLinkTaglet` at all (AFAIK it has some issues for java 8/11 compilation)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m not sure that it should be part of this ticket. it could be if we decide to move javadoc:jar goal for &lt;em&gt;prepare-package&lt;/em&gt; phase. But it smells, this phase is designed for some operations (filtering, exploding, replacing, etc) on files before actual packaging (generating of .jar).&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17273758" author="alex_pl" created="Thu, 28 Jan 2021 14:05:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=mmuzaf&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;mmuzaf&quot;&gt;mmuzaf&lt;/a&gt;, AFAIK all issues with `IgniteLinkTaglet` have been resolved. Why should we remove it? How it&apos;s related to the current ticket?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17276156" author="timonin.maksim" created="Mon, 1 Feb 2021 09:06:39 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=Pavlukhin&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;Pavlukhin&quot;&gt;Pavlukhin&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alex_pl&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alex_pl&quot;&gt;alex_pl&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=mmuzaf&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;mmuzaf&quot;&gt;mmuzaf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ve prepare a PR &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;, could you please review it? On my laptop usage of this profile significantly reduces the time of `mvn package` command. Without the profile, it took 4m27s, but with it just 2m24s.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/8735&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/8735&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17276953" author="pavlukhin" created="Tue, 2 Feb 2021 08:47:53 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=timonin.maksim&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;timonin.maksim&quot;&gt;timonin.maksim&lt;/a&gt;, thank you for your effort! Figures look very promising to me but unfortunately I cannot do thorough review so far. I hope folks will step in.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17277749" author="timonin.maksim" created="Wed, 3 Feb 2021 07:16:01 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=alex_pl&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;alex_pl&quot;&gt;alex_pl&lt;/a&gt;&#160;hi! could you please review it?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17277810" author="alex_pl" created="Wed, 3 Feb 2021 08:41:35 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=timonin.maksim&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;timonin.maksim&quot;&gt;timonin.maksim&lt;/a&gt;, sure, I&apos;ll have a look tomorrow.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17279356" author="ignitetcbot" created="Fri, 5 Feb 2021 05:43:24 +0000"  >&lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; style=&quot;border-color: #ccc;border-style: dashed;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;panelHeader&quot; style=&quot;border-bottom-width: 1px;border-bottom-style: dashed;border-bottom-color: #ccc;background-color: #D6F7C1;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Branch: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;pull/8735/head&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; Base: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;master&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; : No blockers found!&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; style=&quot;border-color: #ccc;border-style: dashed;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;panelHeader&quot; style=&quot;border-bottom-width: 1px;border-bottom-style: dashed;border-bottom-color: #ccc;background-color: #F7D6C1;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Branch: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;pull/8735/head&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; Base: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;master&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; : No new tests found!&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=5856785&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_RunBasicTests&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;TeamCity &lt;b&gt;--&amp;gt; Run :: Basic Tests&lt;/b&gt; Results&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
